# Copy to .env next to docker-compose.yml. .env is gitignored; never commit it.
# Precedence is environment -> file -> default.

# Required. Pi refuses to start without it. At least 16 characters.
#   echo "PI_ADMIN_KEY=$(openssl rand -base64 24)" >> .env
PI_ADMIN_KEY=

# Optional. Where sessions and execution history live. Back this up: it is the
# transcript, and MemoryGate's evidence cites message ids from it.
# PI_DB_PATH=/data/pi.db

# Optional. The model Pi talks to, and where.
# PI_OLLAMA_URL=http://ollama:11434
# PI_MODEL=qwen3:4b

# Optional. The action boundary. Without a key Pi acts on nothing and says so
# in /health as not_configured. Long-term memory requires the separate settings below. Issue a
# scoped execution key in ToolGate; Pi is never given more scope than the tools
# it is meant to reach.
# PI_TOOLGATE_URL=http://toolgate-api:8010
# PI_TOOLGATE_KEY=

# Optional. Timeouts in seconds. The local one is generous on purpose: local
# inference on modest hardware genuinely takes minutes, and a timeout that
# fires on a model that is still thinking turns "slow" into "failed", which is
# a lie about what happened.
# PI_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_S=600
# PI_HOSTED_TIMEOUT_S=180
# PI_TOOLGATE_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Optional. Prepended to every conversation.
# PI_SYSTEM_PROMPT=You are Conker.

# Optional. Hosted models through OpenRouter, used only when a turn
# escalates. Without it Pi answers locally and says so.
# PI_OPENROUTER_KEY=

# Optional. Off means free models only, enforced in code rather than
# left to configuration. Set to 1 to spend deliberately.
# PI_ALLOW_PAID_MODELS=

# Long-term memory: configure all three together. See docs/memory.md.
# PI_MEMORYGATE_URL=http://memorygate-api:8020
# PI_MEMORYGATE_INGEST_KEY=
# PI_MEMORYGATE_READ_KEY=
# PI_MEMORYGATE_AGENT_ID=agent_pi_operator
# PI_MEMORYGATE_TIMEOUT_S=5
